# Project context

Public campaign site for **Micky Ruiz** (Pueblo Libre 2027–2030). Repo: `projecto-municipal`.

## People

| Who | Role |
|-----|------|
| **Anthony** | Engineer / Cursor driver. Can change architecture, deploy, DB. |
| **Miki** | Candidate / content owner. Learning GitHub. Does **not** write code. |

When helping Miki: plain language (Spanish OK), no jargon, never ask him to edit TypeScript.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind
- tRPC + Drizzle + Postgres (optional — site ships without DB)
- NextAuth optional (Discord)
- pnpm only (`packageManager` in `package.json`)
- Deploy: Vercel → `tp00012x/projecto-municipal`

## Where content lives (prefer these for copy/image edits)

| Change | File / folder |
|--------|----------------|
| Name, slogan, email, hero framing | `src/data/site.ts` |
| Proposals text | `src/data/propuestas.json` |
| Team / gallery photos | `public/gallery/` |
| Hero video (web-optimized) | `public/videos/` |
| Page composition | `src/app/CampaignSite.tsx` + `src/components/` |

## Non-negotiables

- Do **not** commit `.env` or secrets.
- Do **not** commit the huge source hero mp4 (`polideportivo-mama-ocllo.mp4`); only the web clip.
- Do **not** require `DATABASE_URL` / `AUTH_SECRET` for a public deploy.
- Prefer systematic boundary fixes over hacks (see `systematic-fixes.mdc`).
- Never merge PRs without explicit confirmation after CI (see `no-auto-merge.mdc`).
